-- Re-enables the AI cron jobs paused by 20260931150000 for flow testing.
-- KEEP THIS FILE DISABLED until every gate below holds (Spec 8; research 06
-- F15 (1), row 8; plan review I16, §6.3). Renaming it to .sql and pushing
-- it is an owner step.
--
-- Resume gates:
--   [ ] Suppression: relationship_ai_suppressed is tested (any tier, 180-day
--       window, either member's positive private check, expiry) and every
--       job honours it: analyse-message, analyse-session, compute-pulse,
--       refresh-love-map, request_verdict_generation, generate-verdict and
--       the ai-sessions shared window (empty when suppressed). Understand
--       and Assist deliberately do not refuse on suppression (a blanket
--       refusal would itself be the tell); their pre-check handles the
--       dangerous inputs.
--   [ ] A failed suppression read defers: the code never sets messages aside or cancels a job on an unreadable answer
--       (analyse-message returns 'deferred'; generate-verdict leaves the
--       job queued).
--   [ ] The co-framing line ships on the Verdict watch areas and on any
--       pattern surface that is routed.
--   [ ] The adversarial Verdict suite passes
--       (supabase/functions/generate-verdict/adversarial.test.ts).
--   [ ] Hostility signals stay off: chat_hostility_signals_enabled = false
--       until clinical sign-off.
--   [ ] The cost ledger is live: ai_provider_calls receives rows and
--       ai_cost_per_relationship reads them; couple-scoped calls carry their
--       relationship (this should return 0 for couple jobs):
--         SELECT fn, count(*) FROM public.ai_provider_calls
--         WHERE relationship_id IS NULL
--           AND fn NOT IN ('analyse-journal-entry', 'generate-healing-portrait',
--                          'generate-healing-post-mortem')
--         GROUP BY fn;
--   [ ] Flow-testing data is purged or verified empty (owner runs, in the
--       production SQL editor, before renaming this file):
--         SELECT count(*) FROM public.patterns;           -- expect 0
--         SELECT count(*) FROM public.analysis_sessions;  -- expect 0
--         SELECT count(*) FROM public.pulse_scores;
--       pulse_scores records no chat weight, so any row computed while chat
--       analysis ran during flow testing may carry chat signals: delete
--       those (or all, if every row is test data) before resuming.
--   [ ] Flags: none of private_safety_check, conflict_toolkit or
--       chat_hostility_signals_enabled was flipped outside the migrations
--       without its draft content being signed off (the launch test cannot
--       see a flag flipped outside the migrations).
--   [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY is set (supabase secrets list): without it
--       callGeminiJson returns null and every job produces its boilerplate
--       fallback silently.
--   [ ] The Verdict cron stays off: generate-verdict-monthly is not
--       scheduled here; a Verdict is generated only on request.
--
-- refresh-love-map-weekly was never paused and calls no provider: it is
-- already running. Schedules are the originals from 20260907120000 and
-- 20260830120000. For local testing use supabase/sql/dev_resume_ai_jobs.sql.

SELECT cron.schedule(
  'analyse-message-backlog', '* * * * *',
  $$ SELECT public.invoke_edge_function('analyse-message'); $$
);

SELECT cron.schedule(
  'analyse-session-sweep', '7,37 * * * *',
  $$ SELECT public.invoke_edge_function('analyse-session'); $$
);

SELECT cron.schedule(
  'compute-pulse-weekly', '0 7 * * 0',
  $$ SELECT public.invoke_edge_function('compute-pulse'); $$
);
